{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): I do apologise for the delay, Doctor. The traffic in from Bray was very heavy, and then the rain came on.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): You're in now. Sit there.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Wipers were going the whole way. You'd swear it was November.",
  "[SEG0004] person_4 (NURSE): I'll just take the blood pressure while ye get settled, alright?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes, of course. Thank you.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (NURSE): 148 over 86. Pulse 72. That's today's reading.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. What brought you in?",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (PATIENT): Well, Doctor, I have been getting a spinning feeling. It only lasts a few seconds, umm, when I turn over in the bed, or if I look up.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Since when?",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (PATIENT): Since last week. Last Tuesday, I think. It came on quite suddenly.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nausea with it?",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes. There is a sick feeling in the stomach when the spinning comes. I have not actually vomited.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hearing loss?",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pain in the ear?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (PATIENT): No. It is not painful.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ringing?",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): Not really. Never.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Blood pressure tablets, yes?",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes, Doctor. I have had high blood pressure for about eight years. I take, err, amlodapine, five milligrams, once a day.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Chest pain with the spins?",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Not that either.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Headaches?",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. Uh, a mild headache in the morning, perhaps twice a week. Not with the spinning, I should say.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Double vision? Slurred speech? Weakness in an arm or a leg?",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (PATIENT): No. None of those.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Her sister is on metformin for the sugar, and she was at her to get checked. I told her that's a different thing altogether.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (PATIENT): I would never take my sister's tablets, Doctor. That medicine is hers.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fullness in the ear?",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Did ye catch the hurling on Sunday at all? Kilkenny were very sharp in the second half. My nephew was up in the stand, and he said the wind nearly took the programme out of his hand.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (PATIENT): I only heard the end of it on the radio, while I waited for the kettle. It sounded very close. A fine match, by all accounts.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He said the drive back from Nowlan Park took three hours, and the chips were stone cold. Worse than the rain we had coming in.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. I'll do a positional test. Lie back, head to the right, quick as you can.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (PATIENT): Oh. Yes. The room spun just then. It has settled now, thank you.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): Eyes flicked and it stopped inside twenty seconds, loose crystals in the inner ear. I'd call it benign positional vertigo, provisional. Do the Epley morning and night for ten days. Back in a fortnight, and the nurse will leave you the sheet.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (PATIENT): Thank you, Doctor. I shall do the exercise carefully, and I will come back in a fortnight."
 ],
